Sval: the stack's frame list leaves aria-activedescendant off until a frame has focus

The debugger's Frames component, which the Browser Console uses to show an
error's stack, starts with currentFrame "" and renders it as
aria-activedescendant="". An empty idref names no element, and with
accessibility on, resolving it calls GetElementById("") and logs "Empty
string passed to getElementById()" against the console's own document, once
per stack shown. The component is Mozilla's, so no chrome API reaches it.

diff --git a/devtools/client/debugger/src/components/SecondaryPanes/Frames/Frames.js b/devtools/client/debugger/src/components/SecondaryPanes/Frames/Frames.js
index bdd314f545..cdefbf75b4 100644
--- a/devtools/client/debugger/src/components/SecondaryPanes/Frames/Frames.js
+++ b/devtools/client/debugger/src/components/SecondaryPanes/Frames/Frames.js
@@ -320,7 +320,9 @@ class Frames extends Component {
         onContextMenu: disableContextMenu
           ? null
           : e => this.onContextMenu(e, frames),
-        "aria-activedescendant": this.state.currentFrame,
+        // currentFrame is "" until a frame takes focus, and an empty idref
+        // names no element: leave the attribute off rather than set it empty.
+        "aria-activedescendant": this.state.currentFrame || null,
         "aria-labelledby": "call-stack-pane",
         role: "listbox",
         tabIndex: 0,
